  the pigs was one of the few decisions  that she made of her own will since  almost every other decision in her life  was forced upon her by her oppressors  and of course as symbolic as this  decision to free the pigs was emir  nearly paid for it with her life however  once amir gains the power of the titans  we have to start looking at her in a  different way even though up to that  point she was clearly a victim of the  aldians once she gains the ability to  become a giant titan she is no longer  just a victim even if we assume that  emir's first few titan transformations  might have been hazy and she may not  have been fully in control we know that  eventually she did gain excellent  control of her titan form because she  was able to use her titan to build  bridges roads and other structures these  are complex projects that required emir  to have a precise control of her titan  form so even though she started out as a  slave after gaining the ability to  become a titan emir was no longer at the  mercy of her aldian captors she could  have used her titan power to crush her  captors if she had wanted to or if she  didn't want to spill any blood she could  have just used her giant titan to escape  from the aldians the ancient aliens of  that era didn't possess any sort of  weapon that would stand a chance against  emir's titan form and since at this  point emir had all nine titan shifter  powers inside of her there were no other  titans who could challenge her as far as  physical power was concerned the aldians  were now at the mercy of emir not the  other way around and yet emir decided to  stay with the aliens to become king  fritz's wife and to use her titan form  to destroy the enemies of eldia this  means that she committed horrible acts  and killed countless people in order to  expand and maintain the aldian empire  among the countless people that she  killed were enemy soldiers but some of  the victims were certainly just innocent  civilians who had nothing 