ot an excuse for hurting  innocent people a traumatic past is not  an excuse for hurting innocent people  and a manipulative spouse is not an  excuse for hurting innocent people at  the end of the day emir fritz is  certainly a victim in many ways but she  is not just a victim she is also a  villain as i mentioned earlier when i  first read the ending of attack on titan  the one that included the extra pages i  thought that amir fritz was a poorly  written character because i kept  thinking of her as just a helpless  victim and someone whom i was supposed  to sympathize and empathize with i only  realized later that she is not a  helpless victim she stopped being  helpless the moment she gained the  ability to turn into a gigantic monster  at will and she stopped being a victim  the moment she consciously chose to use  her titan power to kill other people on  behalf of king fritz emir is a victim  who made the choice to become a villain  even though there are mitigating factors  that we have to keep in mind including  her tragic past and the emotional and  psychological pressures that she faced  from king fritz but still these  mitigating factors do not absolve emir  of her guilt  after all we know that emir wasn't just  completely brainwashed into thinking  that what the aldians were doing was  justified don't forget that she  willingly decided to break the rules  that the aldians had imposed on her by  releasing those pigs if she had been  brainwashed she would have just accepted  all of the rules without question but  emir released the pigs because she knew  that what the aldians were doing was  wrong and releasing the pigs was her own  symbolic form of protest it was a  symbolic statement about how she and the  other enslaved people were being treated  by their captors and yet even though she  clearly knew that what the aldians were  doing to other people was wrong she  chose to support and enable them because  she loved king fritz she even left her  own children at king fritz's mercy  because she chose to die protecting him  and we all know how that turned out then  after waiting for nearly 2 000 years for  aaron to liberate her from her servitude  inside the paths emir willingly  supported and enabled aaron's plan to  destroy the world killing the vast  majority of the world's population in  the process aaron told her that they  should destroy this cruel world in order  to attain true freedom and again she had  no issue with ending countless innocent  lives in order to get what she  personally wanted we know that she  watched all these innocent people die  during the rumbling and yet she didn't  really seem to have a huge problem with  it at the end of the day she doesn't  seem to value human life any more than  king fritz himself did so if aaron is a  villain and many people have argued that  he is then emir is certainly one as well  in the end emir stops the rumbling after  seeing mikasa killing aaron despite  being in love with him this act shows  amir that just like mikasa she too can  break out of the living nightmare that  was her love for king fritz but while i  can appreciate the fact that amir's life  was in many ways a living nightmare did  she really need to see mikasa killing  aaron to realize that king fritz was a  bad person and that killing millions of  innocent people on his behalf was a bad  thing no she did not need mikasa to come  to this conclusion she knew the truth a  long time ago and that is why she  decided to free those pigs  but instead of sticking to the  principles she held even before becoming  a titan the titan emir chose to support  a villain and thus she chose to become a  villain herself the story of emir fritz  is not the story of a victim who had no  agency in her life and who was just  being manipulated by everyone rather it  is the story of a victim who willingly  chose to become a villain and that is  the most tragic aspect of this entire  tale emir was a victim of abuse who  decided to join the ranks of her own  abusers and wreak havoc upon the world  killing millions of innocent people in  the process  and so rather than being a poorly  written victim character as i initially  thought she was she is actually a pretty  well written and pretty effed up villain  character  what do you guys think of emir fritz as  a character and do you agree with my  assessment that she was actually one of  the most messed up villains in attack on  titan don't forget to leave your  feedback down in the comments below if  you guys enjoyed this video and you want  to see more videos like it in the future  just leave a quick like it only takes a  second but it helps with that youtube  algorithm and if you're new to animal  pro or maybe you've been watching our  videos but you just haven't taken the  time to subscribe yet remember that  subscribing and hitting that  notification bell is a very real and  very important way of directly  supporting this channel you can also hit  me up on twitter and instagram at  animeopror i want to give a big thank  you to all of our anime uproar patrons  for making videos like this one possible  special thank you to kyle salisbury this  man is an absolute mad lad and a  disciple of lord to ego himself and i  can't forget all of our the one tier  patrons the ones who rise above all  other clans including alpha sigma in  grata algital pate heffa the red-haired  fox hinokami and water the toasted chi  cory mcgowan spidey left tanel tungsten  tarkis big buddhist and jeremy cummings  finally thank you also to our pro hero  tier patrons including the one and only  gilgamesh steelers angel cruz alicia  octor bonnie parks joy and garcia boy  games kaido might be a duck jessica  rabbit jeremy phillips and alivania if  you enjoy our videos and you feel that  they provide value for you consider  supporting us on patreon even a single  dollar will give you access to our  patron exclusive discord and your name  will appear in our videos along w